  "gloss": {
    "en": "Optionally (Śākalya), a padānta ik vowel before a dissimilar following vowel (asavarṇa ac) remains in its natural form, and the ik is (if needed) shortened (hrasva).",
    "sa": "In saṃhitā at a pada boundary, if the left ends in ik (i/ī/u/ū/ṛ/ṝ/ḷ/ḹ) and the next begins with a vowel that is not savarṇa, Śākalya allows prakṛtibhāva (no yaṇ substitution) and sets the ik to hrasva; alternative derivation applies 6.1.77 (yaṇ)."
  },
